// Did a WAF exclusion actually take effect? One row per day per rule per matched variable, with
// how many of those matches ended in a block.
//
// Loaded by Search-MsecLogAnalytics -Subject Waf -Name ExclusionCheck -WorkspaceName <ws>.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS. An exclusion is deployed and someone asks "is it working?". The obvious
// check - "are there still matches on that rule" - answers the wrong question twice over, and
// this query exists to answer it properly.
//
// A MATCH IS NOT A BLOCK, AND ON CRS 3.x MOST RULES NEVER BLOCK ANYTHING. The OWASP Core Rule
// Set is ANOMALY SCORING: an individual rule such as 932115 or 941101 logs Action="Matched" and
// adds to a score, and a separate rule - 949110 "Inbound Anomaly Score Exceeded" - logs
// Action="Blocked" once the total crosses the threshold. So a rule you excluded can show zero
// blocks for its whole life and still be the reason a request was blocked, and conversely its
// matches can continue harmlessly if the score never reaches the threshold. Measured on one
// gateway: 932115 and 941101 logged Blocked=0 on every single day across a week, while 949110
// blocked 58-73 requests a day on the same host.
//
// THE REAL TEST OF AN EXCLUSION IS THAT THE MATCH COUNT ON THE EXCLUDED VARIABLE GOES TO ZERO,
// not that blocks stop. If matches continue on the variable you excluded, the exclusion did not
// apply - wrong selector, wrong match operator, wrong rule set, or not deployed yet. Pair this
// with BlockedAuth.kql, which shows whether real requests are still being blocked.
//
// Edit the Vars list to whatever the exclusion covers. Case matters in the log text, so both
// casings are checked.
// NO TIME FILTER HERE - the window is -Days (or -Timespan) and the service applies it
// server-side. A window baked into the file is invisible at the call site and silently
// INTERSECTS with the one the caller asked for, so -Days 30 would quietly return 14.
let Vars = dynamic(["redirectUri", "referer", "Referer"]);
AGWFirewallLogs
| extend Detail = strcat(tostring(DetailedData), " ", tostring(DetailedMessage))
| mv-apply V = Vars on (
    where Detail contains tostring(V)
    | project MatchedVar = tostring(V)
  )
| summarize Events = count(),
            Blocked = countif(Action == "Blocked"),
            Hosts   = make_set(Hostname, 5),
            Clients = dcount(ClientIp)
        by Day = format_datetime(bin(TimeGenerated, 1d), "yyyy-MM-dd"), RuleId, MatchedVar
| order by Day asc, Events desc
